<h1>Matt Brewer</h1>
<p>Candidate for Mayor, Chicago, on the ballot February 23, 2027</p>
<p><a href="https://mattbrewer.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign website</a></p>
<p><a href="https://mattbrewer.com/priorities" rel="nofollow noopener">Matt Brewer&#39;s campaign lists four priorities: affordable housing, business and jobs, public safety, and education. Tap here to read them on his site, then come back to comment.</a></p>
<h2>AI summary</h2>
<h3>The platform</h3>
<p>Housing: Make it easier to build homes at every price point, put vacant land back to use, protect renters from displacement, and help homeowners on fixed incomes stay put.</p>
<p>Growth: Grow the tax base with more residents, businesses, and jobs instead of raising taxes, and tie job training to the employers the city recruits.</p>
<p>Safety: Well-trained, accountable police who solve more crimes, continued police reform, and every city service concentrated on the blocks with the most violence.</p>
<p>Schools: Early help for students who fall behind, and a plan for college, a trade, or a job for every CPS graduate.</p>
<h3>Next to the other candidates</h3>
<p>Only Brewer: Concentrating all city services, not only police, on the neighborhoods with the most violence.</p>
<p>Taxes: Mendoza, Kelly, and Brewer say relief comes from a bigger tax base. Holberg and Wilson promise lower taxes, and Carlisle proposes a new income tax tied to pension reform.</p>
<p>Renters: Quigley rejects new rent restrictions. Brewer and Cardenas stress protecting renters from displacement.</p>
<p>Not covered: Pensions and transit, which most other candidates address.</p>
